<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amulius</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amulius is a legendary king of Alba Longa in Roman tradition, who seized the throne from his elder brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/numitor">Numitor</a>. To prevent rivals, he made Numitor's daughter Rhea Silvia a Vestal Virgin, and when she bore the twins <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus">Romulus</a> and Remus he ordered them to be drowned. According to the legend the twins survived, grew up, killed Amulius and restored Numitor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amulius.jpg" alt="Amulius" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Constantine Manasses · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:21-manasses-chronicle.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
